  "scope": "Checked nonlinear Euler foundations, not a completed solver-optimality theorem. The actual Rusanov step has positivity/conservation; a separate principal map has frozen and conditional variable-coefficient energy estimates. Exact counterexamples expose varying-metric noncontraction, a failed global diffusion criterion, and noninvariance of the chosen state region for general compression data outside the target family. Actual physical entropy calculus and flux consistency are checked. The alternative existing logarithmic-mean EC+LF flux has face entropy stability and a terminating exact-real one-step halving search, with state-dependent acceptance/retry bounds. Conditional finite-trace entropy loss follows from a periodic Poincare estimate. These results do not prove target-time completion or verify floating-point guards. Differentiable positive periodic Euler fields have proved global entropy and conserved-state integrals. The actual continuous cell-centered tensor-hat reconstruction has nonnegative partition weights, proved integrals, periodic faces, exact center interpolation, region membership, mean preservation and an integral entropy bound. Entropy gaps give necessary physical L1 error lower bounds. Exact global initial averages and a uniform initial entropy excess of at least 1/33 are proved for the entire target parameter family. For an actual smooth periodic Euler solution with those initial data and final exact/grid states in the region, physical reconstruction error e forces normalized final grid excess at least 1/33-320e, without assuming matching numerical and continuum means. The actual cell-average initializer, common smooth existence, uniform numerical trajectories, full spatial/time accuracy upper bound, justified competitor class and matching complete computational-work bounds remain unproved."
